    "body": "Fixes #42765\nFixes #42778\n\nGLM chat templates write a string argument raw. Non-streaming parsing still ran that text through `json.loads`, so a string whose text is valid JSON was rewritten.\n\n`Glm47MoeDetector` turned `\"hello\"` into `hello`. `Glm4MoeDetector` did the same, and also turned `true` into `True`, `null` into `None`, and `1e2` into `100.0`. Streaming already kept the raw text, so the two paths disagreed. `Ling3Detector` inherits the GLM-4 parser.\n\nA string parameter whose text is valid JSON now stays that text. A string that is not valid JSON still follows the existing fallback, including the invalid-escape case that strips one layer of quotes.\n\n`TestGlm4MoeDetector` and `TestGlm47MoeDetector`: 28 passed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37652692360](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37652692360)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37652691692](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37652691692)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37652692358](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37652692358)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
